# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Codify runtime
.codify/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Node / Web UI
node_modules/
ui/dist/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Rust / Tauri
src-tauri/target/
Cargo.lock
# ...but the desktop crate is an end product, not a library: its lockfile pins
# the exact dependency tree the app ships, so it stays tracked.
!src-tauri/Cargo.lock

# IDE & OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling state (not project code)
.freebuff/
# The agent scratch directory. The rest of .claude/ IS tracked — it is project
# code, reviewed like anything else — but this one is per-machine and mode 700.
# It is also covered by a global ignore in ~/.config/git/ignore, and a global
# ignore is a property of one machine: on any clone without it, this private
# directory would be committed by accident.
.claude/.cc-writes/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
# Third-party benchmark snapshots. Absent until `python3 -m benchmarks.vendor` is
# run deliberately, and never committed by accident: the manifest entry (upstream,
# SHA, licence, reason) is the reproducible half. See docs/08-benchmarks.md.
benchmarks/repos/
graphify-out/
coverage/

# Logs
*.log

# Never commit credentials or their fallback store
secrets.json
# ...except the built-in scan profile of that name: a file of regexes for `scan_code`, with no credential in it
# (every rule's example is a made-up string). The line above matched it and it went unnoticed until a clean checkout
# lacked it; `tests/test_builtin_data_is_committed.py` is what keeps that from happening again. The exemption is
# this one path on purpose: any other secrets.json, anywhere, is still ignored.
!engine/builtin_profiles/secrets.json
